# Environment for scripts/ios-fleet (App Store Connect API key).
# Nothing is read from a local secrets folder.  CI exports these three names in the job
# environment.  On a Mac, ship-testflight.sh and asc-api.mjs read them from Infisical
# Fleet-OPS with `fleet-secrets get` when they are not set:
#   /asc   ASC_KEY_ID, ASC_ISSUER_ID, ASC_KEY_P8 (the .p8 contents)
# Never commit real values.
#
# Create key: App Store Connect -> Users and Access -> Integrations -> App Store Connect API
# Role: Admin or App Manager. Download the .p8 once and store it in Infisical.

ASC_KEY_ID=XXXXXXXXXX
ASC_ISSUER_ID=xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx
# Path to a 0600 file holding the .p8 (CI stages one in the runner temp dir).
ASC_KEY_PATH=/path/to/AuthKey_XXXXXXXXXX.p8

# Optional Apple ID path (only if not using API key):
# APPLE_ID=you@example.com
# APP_SPECIFIC_PASSWORD=xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx
